,\"/inputs/6\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The finite-subcover bound via a maximum fails if C is empty, which is allowed by H003. Also the later assertion that compact C is measurable and has finite Lebesgue measure is not proved or an available permitted calculation. Consequently the construction of an integrable dominating b and the deduction of the M006 hypotheses are unsupported.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/3/hypothesis_checks/0\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The actual prose uses compact-subset-of-Euclidean-space implies Lebesgue measurability and finite measure without a listed theorem or local proof. The author-written calculation allowance is only finite-dimensional differentiation and inner-product identities; it cannot supply this measure-theoretic result. The empty-C issue also shows the purported bound is not established in all cases.\",\"locations\":[\"/logic/calculations\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/3/hypothesis_checks/0\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The claimed conclusion is differentiability of E at every positive r with derivative the integral of e_t, and the paragraph claims exactly this conclusion. Its derivation is blocked, but the stated target matches the output statement.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The paragraph fixes arbitrary r>0 and ends by asserting the result for every positive time. No temporary assumption is introduced and then improperly discharged; no branch witness escapes. This scope correctness does not remedy the unsupported bound.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/0\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/output/statement\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"M005, M004, and the stated M006 binding have recognizable intended applications, but the M006 domination and integrable-bound obligations are not met: K is not established when C is empty, and the finite-measure claim used for M008 is unsupported. Therefore M008's finite-measure premise and M006's integrable domination premise have not been justified from this packet. The textual application records do not themselves prove those premises.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/applications/3\",\"/inference/applications/4\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The direct input and output propositions state the substantive formulas and conditions needed to understand this inference without other inference bodies. D001 and D002 give meanings for e and E; the locally chosen interval and domination are argument constructions rather than missing output content.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/inputs/4/statement\",\"/inputs/5/statement\",\"/inputs/6/statement\",\"/output/statement\",\"/definitions/0\",\"/definitions/1\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Several actual objects are introduced in prose (J, C, δ, the finite centers p_i, K, b, F, F′, τ, x) without corresponding inference-local declarations/metadata. Some have an intelligible informal construction, but the required reverse audit cannot treat the inventory as exhaustive; in particular K's witness construction fails in the empty case. r alone has a recorded local declaration.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/0/objects\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inference/applications/0/bindings\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The uses of compactness to obtain finite measure and hence M008 integrability, and the empty-set-sensitive bound construction, have no direct input or prior local proof. These are factual dependencies in the argument, not consequences licensed by the calculation policy. The M006 theorem application is downstream of the missing facts.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/0/hypothesis_checks\",\"/inference/applications/3/hypothesis_checks/0\",\"/logic/calculations\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Sufficiency from this packet alone fails for the located mathematical reasons above. I read the complete packet and the relevant declared Audit A, self-containment, and format rules in this interaction; the only mathematical task material read was packet.json. No external carrier identity or runtime isolation is attested, and source fidelity is outside this review.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/0/hypothesis_checks/4\",\"/inference/applications/3/hypothesis_checks/0\",\"/warning\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"premises\":\"H003 permits a compact C that is empty; the finite subcover of C×J can then have no centers.\",\"conclusion\":\"The claimed bound |e_t(p)|≤1+max_i|e_t(p_i)| and choice of K are established for the selected C.\",\"why_unsupported\":\"For an empty index set, max_i is undefined. The argument provides no separate case or alternate choice of K. Thus the domination required later is not proved in all cases.\",\"first_unsupported\":true},{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"premises\":\"C is compact, and M008 requires its measure to be finite and the set to be measurable.\",\"conclusion\":\"C is measurable and has finite Lebesgue measure, so M008 gives integrability of the constant on C.\",\"why_unsupported\":\"Compactness implies measurability and finite Lebesgue measure is a substantive measure-theoretic fact absent from the listed inputs and local derivation. The permitted calculation policy does not import it.\",\"first_unsupported\":false}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read_